===Etymology 4===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|すき|alt=主基}}

Nominalization of the {{m|ja|連用形|tr=ren'yōkei||continuative or stem form}} of {{der|ja|ojp|-|sort=すく}}-derived verb {{m|ja|次く|tr=suku||to follow, to continue from something, to be next;}}.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref>

The verb form was obsolete even in olden times. Existence of the verb, possibly related to [[次ぐ|''tsugu'']] mentioned above, is inferred from placenames found in the [[w:Man'yōshū|''Man'yōshū'']] and other ancient poetry.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|すき}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|すき}}

# {{lb|ja|sort=すき|Shinto}} at the {{m|ja|大嘗祭|tr=Daijōsai}} and other major [[Shintō]] ceremonies, refers to the group of regional [[representative]]s making [[offering]]s of [[sake]] and [[grain]], who do so after the initial offering

===Etymology 5===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|ついで|alt=序,序で,第,次いで,尋いで,次第,嗣}}

{{IPAchar|/tuɡite/}} → {{IPAchar|/tuide/}}

Sound shift from {{m|ja|次第|tr=tsugite||order, sequence}}, itself originally the {{m|ja|連用形|tr=ren'yōkei||continuative or stem form}} of now-obsolete {{der|ja|ojp|-|sort=ついで}}-derived verb {{m|ja|継ぎつ|tr=tsugitsu||to do things in sequence, to establish an order}}.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|ついで|acc=0|acc_ref=DJR}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|ついで}}

# [[order]], [[sequence]]
# [[follower]], [[successor]]; the [[next]] thing in a sequence
# [[occasion]], [[opportunity]], doing something [[incidental]] to something else

=====Usage notes=====
The ''good opportunity'' sense is more often encountered as {{ja-r|序でに|ついで に}}.

